more clark county school district  students are returning to buildings  tomorrow  for classes in person now this comes  after pre-kindergarten to third grade  students went back earlier this month  8 news now reporter kristen drummond  joins us live in the newsroom tonight  with more on preparations and what to  expect kristen  sasha the district anticipates about 27  thousand students in grades 6  9 and 12 starting hybrid learning  tomorrow it's a very big day following  more than a year of distance education  for secondary school students i'm so  excited to be going back  eager and enthusiastic honestly like an  answer to my prayers  macy beck welcomes taking classes in  person again at sierra vista high school  having conversations with students my  age is exciting but i also just don't  know what it's going to be like and it  is a little bit nerve-racking  what's so nerve-wracking about it going  back to normal just seems  not right in a way but at the same time  it's something that i've wanted  so bad the senior and student body  president expects an adjustment  so to ease those returning she and the  student council decorated parts of the  school  we have like four different hallways  that we deck out in the theme to  have the students get excited about  coming back all middle and high school  buildings making various preparations  before  monday that includes positioning desks  for social distancing  our custodians are phenomenal and they  actually set up our classrooms for us  billy hemberger teaches at spring valley  high school he says  the big concern starting monday the  hybrid schedule  students take two classes in person then  finish the school day remotely online  the morning courses are now an hour and  45 minutes  there's no way to prepare other other  than  for me anyway i'm just going to kind of  do it and learn as  learn as i go are there any concerns  with the new hybrid schedule i'd be  lying if i said it made sense to me  because it doesn't but for beck it beats  the alternative of continuing full-time  distance education  this is what we have to work with then  we'll work with it  the district gave students a choice of  returning to campuses  or not which means continuing full-time  distance education  they are split among three cohorts and  cohort a  is who starts tomorrow reporting live in  the newsroom kristin drummond 8 news now
 

